---
/**
 * After the first proof, the short version: a lead that reads as the opening
 * of a text, then four plain answers (who, what, where, how to reach). Bold
 * run-ins are the only markers; no cards, icons or dividers.
 */
---

<section class="intro frame" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <div class="lead screen centred" data-enter>
    <h2 id="intro-heading">Systems with moving parts</h2>
    <p class="statement">
      I study economic cybernetics, how systems steer themselves through
      feedback, and build alongside it: the database above, the shop a coffee
      brand sells through, and a market where two kinds of trader meet.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="columns screen centred" data-enter>
    <p>
      <strong>Who.</strong> Tudor-Andrei Ifrim, studying Economic Informatics at
      the Faculty of Cybernetics, Statistics and Economic Informatics in
      Bucharest, graduating in July 2028. Co-founder of Aruna Coffee and head of
      the UI/UX division at SiSC. Before university, robotics: three national
      awards and a top-half international placing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What.</strong> Software first: C and C++, C#, Python, and SQL on
      MariaDB and Oracle. Interfaces second: Figma, Illustrator, Photoshop and
      Spline, with motion in Premiere Pro and DaVinci Resolve. Data third:
      inferential and macroeconomic statistics, and models whose results have to
      survive being checked.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Where.</strong> Bucharest, or remote. Open to an internship, a
      part-time role alongside my degree, or a junior position, and available
      now. I work in English (IELTS C1) and Romanian, with some Spanish and
      French.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reach.</strong> Write to{' '}
      <a href="mailto:tudorifrim606@gmail.com">tudorifrim606@gmail.com</a>, or
      find me on{' '}
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tudor-ifrim-697b0b26a/">LinkedIn</a>.
      The code for this site is public on{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/tudor013/portfolio">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Generous air on both sides of the lead: after the dense blueprint above,
     the page breathes before the four columns start. */
  /* Two screens: the lead, then the four columns. Tudor did not want them
     on screen at once. */
  .lead {
    gap: var(--space-6);
    --content: 48rem;
  }

  .statement {
    max-width: 40ch;
    font-size: var(--step-lead);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .columns {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-12) var(--space-8);
  }

  .columns p {
    max-width: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 75rem) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }
</style>
